cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Character Index
message: >-
  If you use this project or its coverage data in academic work, please cite
  it using the metadata below. The index is a dataset that changes, so cite
  the publication you read: every build has an identifier and a date, and the
  site offers a ready-made citation carrying both. The specifications the
  index reads are third-party works released under CC0 and should be cited to
  their own publishers, not to this project.
type: dataset

# The authors of the index and of the data. Polaris Collective maintains the
# project and runs the deployment, and is deliberately not listed here: the
# coverage this index publishes was produced by the runs below, and adding a
# maintainer to the authors of a dataset it did not judge would misattribute
# it. That changes when a publication carries runs of our own.
authors:
  - given-names: Andrés
    family-names: Cotton
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Stults

contact:
  - name: Polaris Collective
    website: 'https://polariscollective.org'

abstract: >-
  A structured index of where published AI behaviour specifications
  address particular model behaviours, built by an LLM panel of judges
  that scores candidate passages from each specification and records
  every citation with a locator resolving to verbatim spec text.

# This fork, which is what the URL below serves. The original stands alone and
# is the one to clone: https://github.com/AndresCotton/ai-character-index
repository-code: 'https://github.com/polariscollective/ai-character-index'
url: 'https://ai-character-index.vercel.app/spec-reader/'
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-08-24'
keywords:
  - AI alignment
  - model specifications
  - behaviour coverage
  - LLM evaluation
